IMPORT prelude

-- Employment Act 1968 (Singapore) -- PART 10, HOLIDAY, ANNUAL LEAVE AND SICK
-- LEAVE ENTITLEMENTS, ss 88 to 89.
--
-- Source: ../../registers/source-bundle/EmA1968.txt
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No
-- pipeline, no independent test pass, no human gate.
--
-- Part 10 is the most answerable Part in the Act: "how many days do I get?" has
-- a number for an answer, and both tables -- the annual leave ladder and the
-- sick leave bands -- are stated in full in the text rather than left to
-- regulations.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: s 90 (offence), and the parts of s 89(3) that define when an
-- employee counts as hospitalised, which turn on prescribed circumstances and
-- on certificates from approved hospitals.

§ `Employment Act 1968 -- Part 10`

§§ `88 -- Public holidays`

-- s 88(1): "Every employee is entitled to a paid holiday AT HIS OR HER GROSS
-- RATE OF PAY on a public holiday that falls during the time that he or she is
-- employed", subject to --
--   (a) substitution of another day by agreement;
--   (b) a public holiday falling on a REST DAY -> the next working day is the
--       paid holiday;
--   (c) a public holiday falling on a day the employee is not required to work
--       -> the employer may pay OR give a day off in substitution.
-- s 88(2): no holiday pay where the day falls during unpaid leave granted at
-- the employee's request.
DECLARE PublicHolidayFacts HAS
    `the day is a public holiday falling during the employment` IS A BOOLEAN
    `another day was substituted by agreement`  IS A BOOLEAN   -- (a)
    `the public holiday falls on a rest day`    IS A BOOLEAN   -- (b)
    `the public holiday falls on a day the employee is not required to work` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (c)
    `the employee is on leave of absence without pay granted at the employee's request` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (2)
    `the employer gave a day off in substitution` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the facts` IS A PublicHolidayFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the employee is entitled to a paid holiday` IF
        `the facts`'s `the day is a public holiday falling during the employment`
    AND NOT `the facts`'s `the employee is on leave of absence without pay granted at the employee's request`
    AND NOT `the entitlement is answered by a substituted day` `the facts`

-- (a) and (c) both allow the employer to answer the entitlement with a day off
-- instead of pay. (b) does not: it moves the paid holiday to the next working
-- day rather than replacing it.
GIVEN `the facts` IS A PublicHolidayFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the entitlement is answered by a substituted day` IF
        `the facts`'s `another day was substituted by agreement`
    OR  `a day off was given for a non-working day` `the facts`

GIVEN `the facts` IS A PublicHolidayFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a day off was given for a non-working day` IF
        `the facts`'s `the public holiday falls on a day the employee is not required to work`
    AND `the facts`'s `the employer gave a day off in substitution`

-- s 88(1)(b): the holiday moves, it is not lost.
GIVEN `the facts` IS A PublicHolidayFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the next working day after the rest day is the paid holiday` IF
    `the facts`'s `the public holiday falls on a rest day`

§§ `88A -- Annual leave`

-- s 88A(1): an employee who has served "NOT LESS THAN 3 MONTHS" is entitled to
--   (a) 7 days for the first 12 months of continuous service;
--   (b) an additional ONE day for every subsequent 12 months;
--   (c) a MAXIMUM of 14 days.
--
-- So the ladder runs 7, 8, 9 ... 14 and stops: 14 days is reached in the eighth
-- year of service and never rises again.
`the first year annual leave entitlement` MEANS 7
`the maximum annual leave entitlement` MEANS 14

DECLARE LeaveService HAS
    `completed months of service with the employer` IS A NUMBER
    `completed 12 month periods of continuous service` IS A NUMBER
    -- s 88A(2): where 3 months are served but 12 are not completed in the year.
    `completed months of service in that year` IS A NUMBER
    -- s 88A(5): the forfeiture.
    `absent without permission or reasonable excuse for more than 20% of the working days` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the service` IS A LeaveService
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the employee qualifies for annual leave at all` IF
        `the service`'s `completed months of service with the employer` AT LEAST 3
    AND NOT `the service`'s `absent without permission or reasonable excuse for more than 20% of the working days`

-- The full-year entitlement, before any proportioning: 7 for the first 12
-- months, plus one for each subsequent 12, capped at 14.
GIVEN `the service` IS A LeaveService
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the uncapped annual leave days` IS
    `the first year annual leave entitlement`
        PLUS (`the service`'s `completed 12 month periods of continuous service` MINUS 1)

GIVEN `the service` IS A LeaveService
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the full year annual leave entitlement` IS
    IF   `the uncapped annual leave days` `the service` GREATER THAN `the maximum annual leave entitlement`
    THEN `the maximum annual leave entitlement`
    ELSE `the uncapped annual leave days` `the service`

-- s 88A(2) and (3): where 12 months are not completed in the year, the
-- entitlement is proportionate to completed months, and a fraction of a day
-- "less than one-half ... must be disregarded", while "one-half or more ... must
-- be regarded as one day". That is round-half-up.
--
-- Done in INTEGER arithmetic, deliberately. `MODULO` on this toolchain does not
-- return the fractional part of a non-integer -- `3.5 MODULO 1` evaluates to 3.5,
-- not 0.5 -- so a floor built that way silently returns its input. On integers
-- it behaves: 42 MODULO 12 is 6. The entitlement in days and the months in the
-- year are both whole numbers, so the division is expressed as a numerator over
-- 12 and rounded from the remainder, which never leaves integer arithmetic.
GIVEN `the numerator` IS A NUMBER, `the denominator` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the proportion rounded half up` IS
    IF   2 TIMES (`the numerator` MODULO `the denominator`) AT LEAST `the denominator`
    THEN `the whole part` `the numerator` `the denominator` PLUS 1
    ELSE `the whole part` `the numerator` `the denominator`

GIVEN `the numerator` IS A NUMBER, `the denominator` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the whole part` IS
    (`the numerator` MINUS (`the numerator` MODULO `the denominator`))
        DIVIDED BY `the denominator`

GIVEN `the service` IS A LeaveService
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the proportionate annual leave days` IS
    `the proportion rounded half up`
        ((`the full year annual leave entitlement` `the service`)
             TIMES `the service`'s `completed months of service in that year`)
        12

GIVEN `the service` IS A LeaveService
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the annual leave days the employee is entitled to` IS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the employee qualifies for annual leave at all` `the service` THEN 0
        IF `the service`'s `completed months of service in that year` AT LEAST 12
            THEN `the full year annual leave entitlement` `the service`
        OTHERWISE `the proportionate annual leave days` `the service`

§§ `89 -- Sick leave`

-- s 89(1) and (2) are one table in two subsections. Service bands, and for each
-- a non-hospitalisation figure and a hospitalisation cap:
--
--   at least 6 months        14 days   /  the lesser of 60 and (14 + days hospitalised)
--   at least 5, under 6      11 days   /  the lesser of 45 and (11 + days hospitalised)
--   at least 4, under 5       8 days   /  the lesser of 30 and ( 8 + days hospitalised)
--   at least 3, under 4       5 days   /  the lesser of 15 and ( 5 + days hospitalised)
--   under 3 months            none
--
-- Every entitlement is "after examination by a medical practitioner" and only
-- "as may be certified by" that practitioner, so the certificate is a condition
-- and the figures below are ceilings, not amounts due.
DECLARE SickLeaveFacts HAS
    `completed months of service with the employer` IS A NUMBER
    `examined by a medical practitioner`        IS A BOOLEAN
    `hospitalisation is necessary`              IS A BOOLEAN
    `days on which the employee is hospitalised` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `the facts` IS A SickLeaveFacts
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the non-hospitalisation sick leave ceiling` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the facts`'s `completed months of service with the employer` AT LEAST 6 THEN 14
        IF `the facts`'s `completed months of service with the employer` AT LEAST 5 THEN 11
        IF `the facts`'s `completed months of service with the employer` AT LEAST 4 THEN 8
        IF `the facts`'s `completed months of service with the employer` AT LEAST 3 THEN 5
        OTHERWISE 0

GIVEN `the facts` IS A SickLeaveFacts
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the hospitalisation annual cap` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the facts`'s `completed months of service with the employer` AT LEAST 6 THEN 60
        IF `the facts`'s `completed months of service with the employer` AT LEAST 5 THEN 45
        IF `the facts`'s `completed months of service with the employer` AT LEAST 4 THEN 30
        IF `the facts`'s `completed months of service with the employer` AT LEAST 3 THEN 15
        OTHERWISE 0

-- "the LESSER of (i) N days in each year; (ii) the aggregate of M days plus the
-- number of days on which the employee is hospitalised".
GIVEN `the facts` IS A SickLeaveFacts
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the aggregate limb` IS
    `the non-hospitalisation sick leave ceiling` `the facts`
        PLUS `the facts`'s `days on which the employee is hospitalised`

GIVEN `the facts` IS A SickLeaveFacts
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the hospitalisation sick leave ceiling` IS
    IF   `the aggregate limb` `the facts` GREATER THAN `the hospitalisation annual cap` `the facts`
    THEN `the hospitalisation annual cap` `the facts`
    ELSE `the aggregate limb` `the facts`

GIVEN `the facts` IS A SickLeaveFacts
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the paid sick leave ceiling in days` IS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the facts`'s `examined by a medical practitioner` THEN 0
        IF `the facts`'s `completed months of service with the employer` LESS THAN 3 THEN 0
        IF `the facts`'s `hospitalisation is necessary`
            THEN `the hospitalisation sick leave ceiling` `the facts`
        OTHERWISE `the non-hospitalisation sick leave ceiling` `the facts`
